  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Finance (BBA). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Refer to the specific major notes below for variations from the Business (lower level) requirements.\n[grid1 fn2] MATH 148 , MATH 152 , MATH 168 and MATH 172 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 140 .\n[grid1 fn3] For those students under ROTC contract, see Requirement 7 of the \"Requirements for a Baccalaureate Degree.\"\n[grid1 fn4] MATH 147 , MATH 151 and MATH 171 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 142 .\n[grid1 fn5] STAT 211 will be accepted in lieu of BUSN 203 .\n[grid2 fn1] Elective courses are open to any course offered for university credit, except ACCT 209 , ACCT 210 , FINC 409 , IBUS 301 , ISTM 209 , MGMT 209 , MGMT 309 , MKTG 409 , SCMT 309 . Additional restrictions may apply; see academic advisor for information. May be taken on a satisfactory/unsatisfactory basis.\n[grid2 fn2] Refer to the major specific paragraph on the Lower-Level Business Program (BUAD). The general elective taken in the fourth year should be reduced by 1 credit.\n[grid2 fn3] Six hours required. A complete list of approved courses is available in the Undergraduate Advising Office. In the BBA curricula, three of the 6 hours of approved international elective courses simultaneously fulfill the university's International and Cultural Diversity Graduation requirement.\n[grid2 fn4] This course is an approved writing-designated (W) or oral communication (C) business course. See your academic advisor for additional information.\n[grid2 fn5] For those students under ROTC contract, see Requirement 7 of the 'Requirements for a Baccalaureate Degree'.\n[grid2 fn6] Any 300- or 400-level accounting course except ACCT 327 and ACCT 328 . Before enrolling in ACCT 489 , students should consult with the finance department advisor.\n[grid2 fn7] Any 300- or 400-level finance course except FINC 341 , FINC 350 , FINC 409 , and FINC 484 .",
